Hayley's Plan: The Double Agent Gambit
\f1\b0 \
Hayley's plan is brutally simple and relies on one key insight: Gerry and Dunhilton hate each other more than they want to capture Eloise.\

\f0\b The Setup:
\f1\b0  Using her police radio and knowledge of military communication protocols, Hayley broadcasts false intelligence on frequencies she knows both forces are monitoring. She poses as a PAPER communications officer and sends contradictory orders:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
To Gerry's TRAMP forces: "Dunhilton's mercenaries have been compromised. They're planning to seize the technology for foreign buyers. Treat as hostile."\
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
To Dunhilton's mercenaries: "PAPER has been infiltrated. Gerry's team has orders to eliminate all witnesses after securing the facility. You're expendable."\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 The Psychology:
\f1\b0  Both men already suspect the other of ulterior motives. Gerry knows Dunhilton operates outside legal boundaries and has his own agenda. Dunhilton knows Gerry would sacrifice anyone to advance his position within PAPER and TRAMPs. Hayley's false intelligence simply confirms their existing paranoia.\

\f0\b The Execution:
\f1\b0  As the two forces close in, they begin treating each other as threats. Positioning becomes defensive rather than offensive. Communications become hostile. When shooting starts, it's not directed at Sublime Point\'97it's Gerry's TRAMPs firing on Dunhilton's mercenaries, with both sides convinced the other has betrayed the mission.\

\f0\b The Genius:
\f1\b0  Hayley doesn't need to defeat either force. She just needs them to defeat each other. While they're locked in fratricidal combat, Eloise and her people can escape through the tunnels. By the time the survivors sort out what happened, Sublime Point will be empty except for booby traps and destroyed research.\
The plan works because it exploits the one thing stronger than their desire to capture Eloise: their mutual distrust and competing agendas. Hayley makes the government's greatest weakness\'97internal power struggles between PAPER, TRAMPs, and private contractors\'97into their downfall.\
